WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.524
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.824 --> 00:00:09.141
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.441 --> 00:00:15.669
Unit seven: Past Continuous (basic). Today you will describe actions in progress in the past.

4
00:00:15.969 --> 00:00:18.587
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.533 --> 00:00:22.894
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:24.554
Was.

7
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.817
Was means the past of am and is.

8
00:00:28.417 --> 00:00:29.418
I was reading.

9
00:00:30.017 --> 00:00:32.216
Your turn. Say: Was.

10
00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:35.894
Was.

11
00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:37.303
Were.

12
00:00:38.317 --> 00:00:39.933
Were means the past of are.

13
00:00:40.517 --> 00:00:41.529
They were playing.

14
00:00:42.117 --> 00:00:44.293
Your turn. Say: Were.

15
00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:47.763
Were.

16
00:00:48.517 --> 00:00:49.332
-ing.

17
00:00:50.317 --> 00:00:53.373
-ing means the ending that shows an action in progress.

18
00:00:53.983 --> 00:00:55.658
Sleeping, running, reading.

19
00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.310
Your turn. Say: -ing.

20
00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:02.017
-ing.

21
00:01:02.783 --> 00:01:03.912
Interrupted.

22
00:01:04.917 --> 00:01:08.321
Interrupted means stopped for a short time by something else.

23
00:01:08.917 --> 00:01:10.800
The phone interrupted my homework.

24
00:01:11.417 --> 00:01:13.872
Your turn. Say: Interrupted.

25
00:01:16.733 --> 00:01:17.897
Interrupted.

26
00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:19.407
While.

27
00:01:20.417 --> 00:01:23.043
While means during the time that something else happens.

28
00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.533
I was reading while she was cooking.

29
00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:28.419
Your turn. Say: While.

30
00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:32.256
While.

31
00:01:33.017 --> 00:01:33.751
When.

32
00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.202
When means at the time that something happens.

33
00:01:37.817 --> 00:01:39.596
I was sleeping when you called.

34
00:01:40.183 --> 00:01:42.209
Your turn. Say: When.

35
00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:45.661
When.

36
00:01:46.417 --> 00:01:47.812
Background action.

37
00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:52.337
Background action means a long action that was in progress.

38
00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.950
Rain was falling in the background.

39
00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:58.284
Your turn. Say: Background action.

40
00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:02.761
Background action.

41
00:02:03.517 --> 00:02:04.645
Past moment.

42
00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:08.636
Past moment means a particular time in the past.

43
00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.308
At eight o'clock is a past moment.

44
00:02:11.917 --> 00:02:14.848
Your turn. Say: Past moment.

45
00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:18.713
Past moment.

46
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:23.186
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:26.758
Visal, what were you doing yesterday at eight o'clock?

48
00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:37.784
I was having dinner. We use was or were and the -ing form for an action in progress at a past moment: I was having dinner. They were playing.

49
00:02:38.883 --> 00:02:40.848
How is it different from the past simple?

50
00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:54.395
The past simple is a short finished action. The past continuous is a longer action in progress. I was reading when the phone rang. Reading was longer and rang interrupted it.

51
00:02:55.483 --> 00:02:56.798
What does while do?

52
00:02:57.883 --> 00:03:08.280
While joins two long actions: I was cooking while my sister was studying. When often joins a long action with a short one: I was sleeping when you called.

53
00:03:09.433 --> 00:03:11.003
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:16.404
Grammar focus: Past continuous: was and were plus verb-ing.

55
00:03:16.704 --> 00:03:17.821
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.517 --> 00:03:20.516
I was having dinner at eight o'clock.

57
00:03:21.417 --> 00:03:23.544
They were playing football while it was raining.

58
00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:26.194
I was reading when the phone rang.

59
00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:34.917
Use was / were + verb-ing for an action in progress in the past. Use when with a short action that interrupts it and while for two long actions.

60
00:03:35.683 --> 00:03:38.847
Be careful! Don't say: I was study at eight.

61
00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.625
Say: I was studying at eight.

62
00:03:42.925 --> 00:03:44.461
Use -ing after was.

63
00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:48.000
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:49.929
What Were You Doing?.

65
00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:53.285
Yesterday at eight o'clock I was having dinner with my family.

66
00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.461
My mother was cooking while my father was reading the news.

67
00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:00.443
I was studying when my friend called.

68
00:04:01.433 --> 00:04:04.327
It was raining, so the children were playing inside.

69
00:04:05.333 --> 00:04:08.482
The past continuous shows a long background action.

70
00:04:09.567 --> 00:04:13.696
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:16.422
I blank TV when you called.

72
00:04:16.722 --> 00:04:20.317
A, watched. B, was watching. C, watching.

73
00:04:23.867 --> 00:04:25.889
The answer is B: was watching.

74
00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:29.166
They blank football at five o'clock.

75
00:04:29.466 --> 00:04:32.991
A, was playing. B, were playing. C, played.

76
00:04:36.533 --> 00:04:38.486
The answer is B: were playing.

77
00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:41.789
She was cooking blank he was studying.

78
00:04:42.089 --> 00:04:44.906
A, when. B, while. C, then.

79
00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:50.130
The answer is B: while.

80
00:04:51.283 --> 00:04:53.074
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:53.374 --> 00:04:58.258
A, I was study at eight.. B, I was studying at eight.. C, I were studying at eight..

82
00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:04.090
The answer is B: I was studying at eight..

83
00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:07.807
According to the reading, who was reading the news?

84
00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:12.050
A, my father. B, my mother. C, my friend.

85
00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.878
The answer is A: my father.

86
00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:22.450
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:23.317 --> 00:05:26.431
Write a sentence about what you were doing yesterday at 8pm.

88
00:05:35.217 --> 00:05:36.636
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:50.237
Yesterday at eight o'clock I was doing my homework. My mother was cooking in the kitchen and my brother was watching TV. I use the past continuous because these actions were in progress at that moment.

90
00:05:50.537 --> 00:05:52.211
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:53.117 --> 00:05:59.043
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and past continuous: was and were plus verb-ing.

92
00:05:59.343 --> 00:06:03.458
Today's value is reflection. Think about what you learned and how you grew.

93
00:06:03.758 --> 00:06:06.306
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

94
00:06:06.606 --> 00:06:09.374
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

